  "interpretation": "<ul><li><p>Elevated ALP levels: Elevated ALP levels can indicate several conditions, including liver diseases such as hepatitis or cirrhosis, bone disorders such as Paget's disease, or certain cancers such as bone cancer or liver cancer.</p></li><li><p>Low ALP levels: Low ALP levels are less common than elevated levels and can indicate a deficiency in vitamin B6, malnutrition, or hypophosphatasia, a rare genetic disorder that affects bone and teeth development.</p></li></ul>",
